      "Name": "body",
      "Html": "\u003Cstyle class=\u0022code-analysis-syntax\u0022\u003E\n.docs-content pre{overflow-x:auto;margin:1rem 0 1.75rem;padding:1.25rem 1.4rem;border:1px solid rgba(20,42,72,.16);border-left:4px solid #0e6fae;border-radius:4px;background:#f7fbfe;color:#10263a}\n.docs-content pre code{white-space:pre;color:inherit;background:transparent;font-size:1rem;line-height:1.65}\n.language-csharp .syntax-comment{color:#587287;font-style:italic}.language-csharp .syntax-string{color:#8a3d12}.language-csharp .syntax-keyword{color:#6542a6;font-weight:700}.language-csharp .syntax-number{color:#096b65}.language-csharp .syntax-type{color:#0a6680;font-weight:600}\n\u003C/style\u003E\u003Cheader class=\u0022docs-page-header\u0022\u003E\u003Ch1\u003E[page[title]]\u003C/h1\u003E\u003Cp\u003EAn API controller must have exactly one business dependency.\u003C/p\u003E\u003C/header\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EWhat the Standard says\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u0026ldquo;Single Dependency\u0026rdquo; \u0026mdash; A controller has one service dependency and does not reach brokers or native dependencies directly. That single dependency keeps the exposure thin and prevents business orchestration from moving into the API layer. \u003Ca href=\u0022https://github.com/hassanhabib/The-Standard/blob/master/3.%20Exposers/3.1%20Communication%20Protocols/3.1.1%20RESTful%20APIs/3.1.1%20RESTful%20APIs.md#31122-single-dependency\u0022 target=\u0022_blank\u0022 rel=\u0022noreferrer\u0022\u003Eread it here\u003C/a\u003E.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EWhy it matters\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003EA controller is an exposure boundary, not a business workflow. Giving it one business dependency keeps HTTP translation thin and prevents endpoint classes from coordinating services, branching over business decisions, or acquiring layer-specific knowledge.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EBad code example\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cpre\u003E\u003Ccode class=\u0022language-csharp\u0022\u003E\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-comment\u0022\u003E// Violates STXAPI001: An API controller must have exactly one business dependency.\u003C/span\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-keyword\u0022\u003Eclass\u003C/span\u003E \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EStudentsController\u003C/span\u003E(\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EIStudentService\u003C/span\u003E students, \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EICourseService\u003C/span\u003E courses) { }\u003C/code\u003E\u003C/pre\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EGood code example\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cpre\u003E\u003Ccode class=\u0022language-csharp\u0022\u003E\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-comment\u0022\u003E// Follows STXAPI001\u003C/span\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-keyword\u0022\u003Eclass\u003C/span\u003E \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EStudentsController\u003C/span\u003E(\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EIStudentService\u003C/span\u003E students) { }\u003C/code\u003E\u003C/pre\u003E"
    }
  ],
